# Which project directories may have their Claude configs auto-backed-up.
#
# HOW THIS WORKS
#   One path prefix per line. `~` is expanded. Blank lines and #-comments ignored.
#   A project file is auto-added to chezmoi only if it sits under one of these
#   prefixes. Anything else under $HOME is ignored.
#
# IMPORTANT — this list widens WHERE we look, never WHAT we back up.
#   Even inside an allowlisted directory, only Claude config files are tracked:
#     - CLAUDE.md
#     - CLAUDE.local.md
#     - anything under a .claude/ directory
#   Your source code, build output, and data are never touched. Adding a 20GB
#   project directory here does not put 20GB in your dotfiles repo.
#
# ALWAYS INCLUDED (no need to list them):
#   ~/.claude/   ~/.codex/   ~/.kimi-code/
#
# To stop tracking something already added:  chezmoi forget <path>
# To see what is tracked:                    chezmoi managed

~/Desktop/projects/
